In `farthest_points`, the relevant evaluations come from the nested generator `rotatingCalipers`. In the nondegenerate branch, it starts with `i = 0` and `j = len(L) - 1`, and each loop iteration first executes `yield U[i], L[j]`. After yielding, the code may increment `i`, decrement `j`, or do one of those based on the hull-edge comparison; there is no condition anywhere that preserves `i <= j`. Because the two indices move independently in opposite directions, the generator can reach states with `i > j` before yielding, so `i <= j` is not an invariant across all evaluations of that yield.

## Answer
{"invariant_exists":false}
